{
 "source": "wowsims/forever d0ba78b81e1e302392cacf5c7d5e7eecb05cf6a0",
 "notes": {
  "positions": "tab = 1-based index of the tree in ui/sim/talents/trees/<class>.json. gen_protos.go transformRawTalentsToTab sorts tabs by name, which for all nine classes equals the in-game order (Arms/Fury/Protection, Holy/Protection/Retribution, ...). row = location.rowIdx + 1, column = location.colIdx + 1. These are NOT a Talent.db2 TierID/ColumnIndex: WoW Forever ships talents as a trait tree, and tools/database/tables.go LoadTraitTalents (~1500-1830) snaps each TraitNode PosX/PosY onto a grid (row = (PosY - minY) / pitch, col = (PosX - tabOrigin) / pitch, tabs split by X gaps). wowsims validates the result against tier rules (5 points per row) and the game prereq arrows, so it is very likely the in-game layout, but it is not verified here against GetTalentInfo(tab, index) tier/column. GetTalentInfo index order is not given by wowsims; match by name or by tier+column.",
  "pctByRank": "pctByRank is the game-file curve (spells_auto_gen.go generatedCurves) the sim reads per rank; pctPerRank is the rank 1 value. Where linear is false use pctByRank.",
  "statNames": "stat / from / to use proto/common.proto Stat names; Health, Mana, BonusArmor are proto stats too. SpiritRegenWhileCasting is a pseudo-stat (PseudoStats.SpiritRegenRateCasting), not a proto Stat.",
  "noEntries": "warrior and rogue have no talent in this data that multiplies or converts a primary/secondary stat (warrior Shield Specialization is block chance, Anticipation is defense skill, rogue Weapon Expertise is expertise).",
  "excluded": "conditional or flat effects left out: priest Spirit Tap (+100% Spirit for 15s after a kill, 20..100% chance), hunter Resourcefulness buff, shaman Ancestral Healing (Ancestral Fortitude +8% armor after a crit heal), druid Predatory Strikes (flat level-based AP in forms), warlock Demonic Knowledge (flat level-based spell damage while a demon is out), shaman Improved Reincarnation.",
  "otherTalentChecks": "Other getTalents() uses in ui/specs that are NOT EP-preset switches: warrior dps presets.ts:24-28 (mortalStrike/bloodthirst pick Arms vs Fury rotation, spec.ts:131/152), paladin retribution spec.ts:18 and inputs.ts:72-116 (rotation and seal inputs), priest dps inputs.ts:15 (shadowform), warlock dps inputs.ts:23-83 (demonicSacrifice/demonicPact), shaman elemental spec.ts:24 (stormstrike warning). Every other spec has a fixed or user-picked EP preset."
 },
